<title>PORTUGAL: Av rate seen 5.39-5.44 pct Portugal bond auction.</title>
<headline>Av rate seen 5.39-5.44 pct Portugal bond auction.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are forecasts by five banks of rates at today's auction of March 2000 fixed rate Portuguese bonds. Results of auction around 1000 GMT.</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>- RATES OFFERED:     Min/Avg/Max	vs	(13 May 1997)</p>
<p>    MIN:	    5,35%/5,37%/5,40%   vs   Last auction:5,44%</p>
<p>    AVG:	    5,39%/5,411%/5,44%  vs   Last auction:5,5013%</p>
<p>    MAX:	    5,44%/5,454%/5,48%  vs   Last auction:5,51%</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>- FULL PLACING:</p>
<p>    Yes: four forecasts	     vs Last auction:9.125 bln esc</p>
<p>No:  one forecast</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Close (9 Jun) on OTC: 5.46 pct</p>
<p>Apr 2000 Bonos: 5.22 pct</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The auction of March 2000 bonds is expected to result in a lower average weighted interest rate than the previous auction due to a positive mood in international markets, notably peripherals, dealers said. Most dealers said they expected that the average weighted rate would come out around 20 basis points above April 2000 Bonos.</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>----Sergio Goncalves, Lisboa Editorial, 351-1-3150035</p>
